<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Interior bids soften.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Interior bids soften.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Basis bids for hard red winter wheat softened at interior locations but remained firm at the Gulf of Mexico, grain merchandisers in the High Plains said Thursday.</p>
<p>Movement was sluggish, however, as producers held out for higher prices.</p>
<p>&quot;I think the producer's still pretty bullish and is thinking that (prices) are going to come back even more,&quot; an Oklahoma dealer said.</p>
<p>Meanwhile, more basis bids were rolled out to the KCBT March contract from KCBT December.</p>
<p>Dealers said there were forecasts for snow or sleet throughout Kansas this weekend.  </p>
